	(text "Signal return, ${dcabc325-b008-4566-9bd8-5d9f33a3ddd9:REFERENCE} pin 2 and shell SH; clamp and bypass return." (at 423.76 72.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "18411c86-75a8-59b6-9c87-2c5b88244251"))
	(text "DIO-A (${dcabc325-b008-4566-9bd8-5d9f33a3ddd9:REFERENCE} pin 1) after ${e48050c4-7c3e-4feb-a8bf-c915c166209c:REFERENCE}: controller TX, this board's RX; SCL or MOSI." (at 423.76 85.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6afb504d-fe1a-5064-846f-db33b199fb73"))
	(text "DIO-B (${dcabc325-b008-4566-9bd8-5d9f33a3ddd9:REFERENCE} pin 4) after ${47e56d03-98c6-43ee-9728-332e5044ac5c:REFERENCE}: controller RX, this board's TX; SDA or MISO." (at 423.76 97.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "dbdd6b60-106a-5e5b-ac76-03f94acfe4ed"))
	(text "Instrument tap of DIO-A through ${e899fcb6-9ded-4f69-8a04-6d774dee2032:REFERENCE} (100 ohm); observe only." (at 423.76 110.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "94f7f1a2-7938-52ca-9c1e-112d54cf95a0"))
	(text "Instrument tap of DIO-B through ${354ce1ed-5d8e-453c-a90d-2659c77a0fab:REFERENCE} (100 ohm); observe only." (at 423.76 123.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b0a378e3-d776-5097-bea5-170de9b80e15"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 138.43) (xy 578.76 138.43)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "54fcae7c-17a7-5742-9207-bf4767247afb"))
	(text "OPERATION" (at 423.76 140.97 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7aa89f5a-f998-58eb-8158-9dedf2b1355e"))
	(text "Pin map of ${dcabc325-b008-4566-9bd8-5d9f33a3ddd9:REFERENCE}: 1 DIO-A, 2 GND, 4 DIO-B, 6 port 5 V; pins 3, 5, 7 and 8 are no-connect. DIO-A carries the controller's TX, SCL or MOSI and is" (at 423.76 145.12 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4bf80140-2118-535f-ab36-d86f918fa5ce"))
	(text "this board's RX; DIO-B is the controller's RX, SDA or MISO and this board's TX (board-interfaces pycontrol-behavior-port.md, the one invariant). Ports" (at 423.76 147.66 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e54c2ffe-7791-5935-925d-3f7aed013cd3"))
	(text "are named by connector position so a board cannot mirror them; cross to RX/TX once, at the MCU sheet." (at 423.76 150.2 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b9d184be-ef10-5562-8b15-5d43ff0de467"))
	(text "Each DIO line passes a 100 ohm series resistor (${e48050c4-7c3e-4feb-a8bf-c915c166209c:REFERENCE} on DIO-A, ${47e56d03-98c6-43ee-9728-332e5044ac5c:REFERENCE} on DIO-B); ${f93728e2-2141-439d-b216-bcf1db600f7d:REFERENCE} (USBLC6-2P6) clamps both lines and the 5 V" (at 423.76 154.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5677a8e1-81ea-5870-8a3b-14e2dc4598f3"))
	(text "node on the connector side of the resistors, so each line routes in one I/O pad and out the other. The controller has nothing in series (its ports carry" (at 423.76 156.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ed72f14c-9385-5cf5-941c-502b68c300f2"))
	(text "only an ESD array), so these resistors are the link's only current limit; 100 ohm into the clamp's 3.5 pF is far below the 8.7 us bit of 115200 8N1." (at 423.76 159.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f45d7a11-fbd8-515f-bc97-e2fbaeaf385e"))
	(text "USBLC6-2P6: 6 V minimum VBUS breakdown, 12 V typical clamp at 1 A 8/20 us, IEC 61000-4-2 level 4 (15 kV)." (at 423.76 161.63 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b78dba0b-c94e-5ea1-a677-d480d793807a"))
	(text "PYC_CONN_5V is the raw pin-6 node, bypassed by ${3a18ddf5-1a49-4a68-9246-f01a86a3a8ad:REFERENCE} (100 nF) and the clamp's upper reference, so pin 6 must be wired for the clamps to" (at 423.76 165.44 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a35882be-c91e-54fd-827d-5e7b00793606"))
	(text "reference; +5V_PYC is the same node through ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} and ${68d4fb06-543a-4879-ba8d-7f948c719952:REFERENCE} (MBR120VLSFT1G, 20 V 1 A Schottky, 0.34 V max at 1 A, 0.6 mA leakage at 25" (at 423.76 167.98 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b9d54a11-f249-51a2-9c0c-43cbbc71c203"))
	(text "C) for diode-ORing with the USB block's +5V_USB. ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} is a polyfuse position: the pyControl port shares one 1.0 A supply with the controller's" (at 423.76 170.52 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a8b56eee-0397-544d-a1cc-59366c2f328b"))
	(text "own regulator and has no per-port fuse, so the stocked 0.36 ohm 1206 is a jumper until a 250 to 500 mA PPTC is in the catalog. ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} and" (at 423.76 173.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "932e7f6c-6d4a-5ed6-bf6c-b06815e75fa5"))
	(text "${68d4fb06-543a-4879-ba8d-7f948c719952:REFERENCE} may be DNP on a board that takes no port power." (at 423.76 175.6 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7f0188ee-c8d4-59f1-9a04-2944351ad37f"))
	(text "Not every port has a UART: Breakout 1.2 has one on ports 1, 3 and 4 only, the H7 breakout routes seven but the firmware declares none yet" (at 423.76 179.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "06cce799-9a66-551e-90f4-e77c98574907"))
	(text "(pycontrol-behavior-port.md). Pin 5 is DIO-C on some ports and a POW-C sink-driver output on others, which is why it stays unconnected. The" (at 423.76 181.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "46af9198-05b5-55c4-8750-8ff29af7512c"))
	(text "placing board records the port assignment and uses a UART-capable port; the pin map is cited from the syringe-pump module and H7 breakout" (at 423.76 184.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "aac96373-450e-5b34-b65c-39c129dabf91"))
	(text "schematics, not bench-verified." (at 423.76 187.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5a277cd9-9a53-5b34-aca7-b7a54fd41e61"))
	(text "${e899fcb6-9ded-4f69-8a04-6d774dee2032:REFERENCE} and ${354ce1ed-5d8e-453c-a90d-2659c77a0fab:REFERENCE} (100 ohm) tap DIO-A and DIO-B for the instrument port (INSTRUMENT class), observe only; these are the block's own signals," (at 423.76 190.84 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "96aa38e0-61e1-5393-a134-d06ae5ea9c91"))
	(text "so the taps live here (convention 14)." (at 423.76 193.38 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "224caaa8-f9c2-59d1-a08d-a585924d7d3f"))
	(text "Beyond the two instrument taps, the only schematic difference from the horizontal block: the jack is shielded and both shell legs (pad SH, joined by" (at 423.76 197.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "0968f49e-2f40-5528-93ba-ef98e402c656"))
	(text "the shell) are tied to GND here; break that tie and terminate through a pad/cap network if the cable shield must float from signal ground." (at 423.76 199.73 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4014f852-394a-530f-8aeb-af87e88cf930"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 211.16) (xy 578.76 211.16)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "34a59e42-36d5-564d-83ab-68c64e779090"))
	(text "DESIGN NOTES" (at 423.76 213.7 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c73b20fb-8136-5698-b6b8-9412385fa39d"))
	(text "DIO_A (pin 1) is ALWAYS the host's driving line: UART TX, I2C SCL, SPI MOSI." (at 423.76 217.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "cbcc5ad4-8938-523d-bc9f-b704b8950891"))
	(text "▎ DIO_B (pin 4) is the host's input: UART RX, I2C SDA, SPI MISO. No exceptions ▎ on any pyControl breakout. So DIO_A = this board's RX." (at 423.76 220.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f82b2265-0f28-5872-9c3c-916cfea4ef1a"))
	(text "▎ Breakout 1.2 UART ports: 1 (UART4), 3 (USART1), 4 (USART3). I2C only on 3, 4." (at 423.76 222.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "bef70316-8f3b-5174-88d7-3c058f0830c6"))
	(text "▎ H7 breakout UART ports: 1,2,3,4,5,9,10. I2C on 1, 6. SPI on 7, 8." (at 423.76 225.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "97687a52-cd3d-5a35-9cc3-23dbf30f2927"))
	(text "▎ Breakout 1.2 analog-in on DIO_A/B works on ports 1 and 6 ONLY (2/3/4/5 are ▎ GPIOB6-13, no ADC channel). Port 6 DIO_B is the same net as" (at 423.76 228.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "a303660b-bda8-51d4-a9a8-c60a59cc0fbd"))
	(text "BNC-2." (at 423.76 230.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5026a269-789b-57e8-b868-4ec9e6a717cb"))
	(text "▎ DIO_C (pin 5) is NOT 5V tolerant where it is a DAC (PA4/PA5). DIO_A/DIO_B are FT." (at 423.76 233.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "31be77d3-08ae-51d2-9d87-feddcd366eec"))
	(polyline (pts (xy 423.76 244.52) (xy 578.76 244.52)) (stroke (width 0.254) (type default)) (fill (type none)) (uuid "005c56be-f112-5426-b2a9-b72ca67227dc"))
	(text "DESIGN CONTRACT" (at 423.76 247.06 0) (effects (font (size 1.6 1.6) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3c2356da-ce01-5e54-893c-a97aadec6a21"))
	(text "pyControl behavior-port boundary on a VERTICAL, top-entry SHIELDED 8P8C RJ-45 jack: Molex 855085001, OW-CONN-RJ45-8P8C-THT-VERT, Cat5e," (at 423.76 251.21 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "7356088f-54d7-5664-8e20-4cd59c88f655"))
	(text "16.5 mm tall, 1.5 A per contact, through-hole signal contacts plus two through-hole shell legs and two locator pegs. NOT Ethernet and no magnetics" (at 423.76 253.75 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4b4e2f5f-2eef-5afa-9ba6-e95de25414bc"))
	(text "— the jack is a connector family, nothing more. The same front end as the horizontal pycontrol_behavior_port_rj45_boundary block: pin map 1 DIO-A," (at 423.76 256.29 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d85096fe-b80a-51cd-aa63-4f378edce981"))
	(text "2 GND, 4 DIO-B, 6 5V with pins 3, 5, 7, 8 explicitly no-connect; 100 ohm series resistance and a USBLC6-2P6 channel on both DIO lines, with the" (at 423.76 258.83 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "ae6fce96-d1c7-5278-be4d-12014d57d3da"))
	(text "clamp on the connector side of the resistors and each line routing in one I/O pad and out the other; 100nF on the raw 5 V node; and the same 5 V" (at 423.76 261.37 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f7a28adf-fa27-5967-af81-ee3a4b751faf"))
	(text "branch exposing PYC_CONN_5V, the raw pin-6 node, and +5V_PYC, the same node through ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} and a MBR120VLSFT1G series Schottky, for" (at 423.76 263.91 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8fa48c72-a62e-52d2-9ae6-1575e90b984b"))
	(text "diode-ORing with other 5 V sources — pair it with usb2_vertical's +5V_USB. WATCH THE DIRECTION: pin 1 DIO-A carries the host's transmit and is the" (at 423.76 266.45 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "62fdf35a-2a57-56e8-91d8-5ee0f12afa6f"))
	(text "DEVICE'S RX; pin 4 DIO-B is the device's TX. Boundary pins are named by connector position, not by direction, so a board cannot mirror them by" (at 423.76 268.99 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "2da4a13d-3b12-5085-95fe-f1c0d48458e1"))
	(text "accident." (at 423.76 271.53 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1bea8ea8-8b1e-5e78-9506-3eb017f17a2a"))
	(text "${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} IS A POLYFUSE POSITION, not protection: the pyControl port supplies a shared 1.0 A that also feeds the controller's own logic regulator, with" (at 423.76 274.07 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "553a3fcd-bf82-5a86-89bb-e98d2c48e718"))
	(text "no per-port fuse, so a fault on the board can reset the experiment controller. Populate a 1206 PPTC holding 250-500 mA when one is in the" (at 423.76 276.61 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "15fa3279-ef20-5827-804c-c6ce586aa964"))
	(text "catalog; the 0.36 ohm resistor is only a stocked 1206 jumper, and the position must be populated or the branch is open. The USBLC6's clamp rail" (at 423.76 279.15 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "77d2da49-0839-5bbc-a394-252a31ef5e66"))
	(text "taps PYC_CONN_5V upstream of ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} so it stays low-impedance and stays referenced if the fuse trips, which also means pin 6 must be present" (at 423.76 281.69 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "e25204c8-67a7-5ada-8591-6d36da8cda2d"))
	(text "for the I/O clamps to have an upper reference. On a board that takes no port power, ${aaadbed3-b7b1-4b40-896d-f506d8dbaf59:REFERENCE} and ${68d4fb06-543a-4879-ba8d-7f948c719952:REFERENCE} can both be DNP. Pin 5 is DIO-C on" (at 423.76 284.23 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "35b186be-fe82-5573-8d20-47fa2938b193"))
	(text "some breakout ports and a POW-C sink driver output on others, so it is deliberately unconnected; do not repurpose it without fixing the port" (at 423.76 286.77 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "655d8caf-63c3-5ac2-8d1b-9a706f24666e"))
	(text "assignment first. The assigned port must be UART-capable." (at 423.76 289.31 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "d29ae29b-4882-55d6-b293-3e7716789ca1"))
	(text "Two schematic differences from the horizontal block. This jack is shielded: both shell legs are pad SH, joined by the metal shell" (at 423.76 291.85 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c3db3713-1c79-5af1-8631-9bd9b4be73f6"))
	(text "(duplicate_pad_numbers_are_jumpers), and this block ties SH directly to GND. If the cable shield ever needs isolating from signal ground, break that" (at 423.76 294.39 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "01a6007b-b96e-5a13-80ac-3d10beac1ba4"))
	(text "tie here and terminate through a pad/cap network instead — the same choice usb2 makes for the USB-C shell. And the DIO lines carry instrument" (at 423.76 296.93 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9e32e52a-5226-5658-908d-00fe9716757f"))
	(text "taps: ${e899fcb6-9ded-4f69-8a04-6d774dee2032:REFERENCE} and ${354ce1ed-5d8e-453c-a90d-2659c77a0fab:REFERENCE} (100 ohm) tap the board side of DIO-A and DIO-B to PYC_DIO_A_INST and PYC_DIO_B_INST, observe only; these are the" (at 423.76 299.47 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5c293676-1691-5d8b-a3e8-787e05ff91bb"))
	(text "block's own signals, so the taps live here. Ports PYC_DIO_A, PYC_DIO_B, PYC_CONN_5V, +5V_PYC and GND keep their names from the horizontal block;" (at 423.76 302.01 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "f11e25f4-0982-5c30-9562-2777ae2f51d0"))
	(text "the two INST taps are added." (at 423.76 304.55 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "af3bacc4-c762-5e7f-b394-0a2ca8f944a0"))
	(text "The land pattern differs completely from the horizontal block, which is why this is a separate block and not a footprint swap. Signal rows are" (at 423.76 307.09 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8ac28fb5-05c9-5ff7-8fd5-3ed1e8b23286"))
	(text "staggered at y = 0 (pins 1, 3, 5, 7) and y = -2.54 (pins 2, 4, 6, 8), 1.27 mm x pitch, 1.4 mm pads on a 0.89 mm drill, against the horizontal" (at 423.76 309.63 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "fd3116d1-6d76-50d8-816a-ea807c41a8f9"))
	(text "43860-0001's y = 1.78 / 0 at 1.02 mm pitch on 1.5 mm pads. PAD ORDER REVERSES: pin 1 sits at x = 0 and ascends in +x to pin 8 at x = 8.89," (at 423.76 312.17 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9620b31c-e98e-5c72-b5c6-c90ae7eb8bc9"))
	(text "where the horizontal starts pin 1 at x = +3.56 and descends. Two SH pads are 2.11 mm on a 1.6 mm drill at y = 9.4, far outboard of the signal" (at 423.76 314.71 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "6494df49-6447-5509-9882-a387bd01e742"))
	(text "rows, and the two 3.25 mm NPTH locators move from y = 4.32 to y = 6.35. No pad lands where it used to. Unlike the tier 1 terminal blocks and" (at 423.76 317.25 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "daefe0ce-8a0e-57de-b57d-4f295b1aea15"))
	(text "usb2_vertical, this footprint GROWS rather than shrinking: courtyard is x -4.66 to 13.55, y -4.70 to 13.10, roughly 18.2 x 17.8 mm, against the" (at 423.76 319.79 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5e83037a-9712-5e25-9405-69fac8cd3d5a"))
	(text "horizontal's x +/-8.00, y -5.84 to 9.65, roughly 16.0 x 15.5 mm, and the body no longer overhangs the board edge, so budget the area before" (at 423.76 322.33 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "9f04b00d-11fc-518b-9941-c012268126d4"))
	(text "placing." (at 423.76 324.87 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "8fd09e6f-86ff-5c64-886b-d89001724d9b"))
	(text "VERIFY PIN 1 PHYSICALLY against the latch and keyway, not against the footprint's local x order, because the two footprints number pads in opposite" (at 423.76 327.41 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "c031ad3a-41bc-5678-9fe7-9f461f9cc3d0"))
	(text "directions and a mirrored 8P8C map produces a silently crossed pyControl port; check against ../mouse-joystick-pcb/docs/pycontrol-port-pinout.md." (at 423.76 329.95 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3aba89e3-d20e-567c-a6da-f3db04dc1688"))
	(text "The two locator holes are not optional — the part will not seat without them, they sit inside the connector body where it is tempting to route, and the" (at 423.76 332.49 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "dcc950ac-2b2b-586c-a4d1-efad52f230d3"))
	(text "shell legs punch every layer, so place all four holes before pouring GND or routing the port. Retention is the reason to prefer this part over the SMD" (at 423.76 335.03 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "db047fde-8ac4-5be7-a876-69ee876e14f1"))
	(text "OW-CONN-RJ45-8P8C-SMD-VERT fallback: insertion and extraction force goes into the board rather than into solder joints, on a rig that gets" (at 423.76 337.57 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "19cc283f-ad2c-574f-a3ca-1d77068eea1a"))
	(text "handled. The cable now leaves perpendicular to the board, so the enclosure in ../mouse-joysticks-mech needs an aperture above the jack plus" (at 423.76 340.11 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "3708a3bf-ea03-513f-b3bd-3b7a6df76664"))
	(text "clearance for the plug body, its latch, and the wire loop, well beyond the 16.5 mm jack height. Not pad-compatible with OW-CONN-438600001 or" (at 423.76 342.65 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "691f960e-be79-5bd2-add1-fb5e63d46925"))
	(text "OW-CONN-RJ45-8P8C-SMD-VERT, and deliberately shares no equiv_group with either." (at 423.76 345.19 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "49217b29-0af9-5eca-8dc0-d8d1eb9207b8"))
	(text "Pinout is schematic-derived from the syringe-pump pyControl module and the pyControl H7 breakout, which agree on all eight positions, but it is" (at 423.76 347.73 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "190dfc00-9583-5085-bd4d-61c2a817ac94"))
	(text "CITED, NOT BENCH-VERIFIED — confirm continuity and cable polarity on real hardware before trusting a populated board. +5V_PYC leaves ${68d4fb06-543a-4879-ba8d-7f948c719952:REFERENCE}" (at 423.76 350.27 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "300483e5-e338-51a9-b25d-9282672dffa0"))
	(text "pad 1 into a port via, where a placing board picks the rail up." (at 423.76 352.81 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "1a4a53f4-1d25-5f45-a168-e2de407d249a"))
